<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="prose fade-in">
            <p>Elephas is run by an experienced engineer who uses AI agents as tools — not as a substitute for judgement. That gives an unusual combination: <strong>a small company's closeness and honesty, with a development team's capacity.</strong></p>
            <p>We build with AI every day, on real deliveries. That's why we know exactly what the tools can do, where they fall short, and how to direct them to results that meet a professional standard.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="fade-in">Five steps, every project</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Understand &amp; specify</h3>
                <p>We start with the business, not the technology. Requirements are documented clearly enough that you, we, and our AI agents all work towards the same goal — it's the foundation for everything that follows.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Build</h3>
                <p>AI agents write code under constant senior direction. What takes a traditional team weeks often takes days — and you see working results as we go.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Review</h3>
                <p>Every line of code is reviewed by an experienced engineer before it becomes part of the delivery. AI's pace, a senior's judgement — never one without the other.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Verify</h3>
                <p>Automated tests run on every change, and user interfaces are visually verified with Playwright: screenshots of every flow, at multiple screen sizes, compared against the design and expected behaviour.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="fade-in">
                <h3>Monitor</h3>
                <p>After launch: monitoring, alerts and ongoing support if you want it. We see problems before your users do.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

